<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diktaean Zeus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dictaean Zeus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diktaean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> was a form of Zeus worshipped in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, linked with the myth of the god's birth and upbringing in a Cretan cave. His main sanctuary lay near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palaikastro">Palaikastro</a>, where the Hymn of the Kouretes was found. Control of the sanctuary and its lands was long disputed between Itanos, Praisos and Hierapytna.</p></div>
